  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Tromso Arctic Surveillance",
  "description": "Contains digital satellite data from the satellites NOAA, Landsat 1-5, and SPOT. The ground truth data/field data are vegetation (reliefs) data, geomorphology, air pollution impact data (long transported/locally), and sea temperature. Atmospheric physics data are ozone data (satellite and ground measurements). Also included are Synthetic Aperture Radar (SAR) data (aircraft, buoys).\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: This data base is now under development and will probably be linked to the United Nations Environmental Program - Global Resource Information Data Base in Arendal, Norway. The date base will also play a role in the Norwegian part of the Arctic Monitoring Program (AMP).",
